      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "This randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled study shows that 20-week fluvastatin treatment induces beneficial changes in the lipid panel and a shift in the fibrinolytic pathway toward activation through a decrease in tissue plasminogen activator antigen. Fluvastatin treatment causes no variation in lipoprotein(a) circulating levels."},
